/*  FUNCTION NAME:      PIPS
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns the pip value (1-6) of a Unicode die face.*/
/*  RETURNS:            number: pip value (1-6) of the die face; lifts over arrays
    PARAMETERS:
        Dice            (Required) A Unicode die face ⚀-⚅ (U+2680-U+2685). Also accepts a range or array of dice - result lifts element-wise. Non-dice or blanks return #N/A.
    EXAMPLE:            =PIPS("⚄") -> 5
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-07-16  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
PIPS = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [Dice],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        result, IFERROR(
                    LET(v, UNICODE(Dice) - 9855,
                        IF((v >= 1) * (v <= 6), v, NA())),
                    NA()),
        result
)
);
